# Task: chebyshev_relu_d2
Degree-2 Chebyshev polynomial approximation of the relu activation on [-4, 4] (benchmarks/chebyshev_ckks).
Inputs: ciphertext `x` (values in [-4, 4]); plaintext scalars: `alpha` = 0.25 (maps x to z = x/4 in [-1, 1]), `one` = 1.0, and c0 ... c2, the Chebyshev coefficients (each one is the same in every slot).
Output: `y` = c0 + sum_k c_k T_k(z), with T0 = 1, T1 = z and T_k = 2 z T_{k-1} - T_{k-2}. The coefficients c1, c2 and c0 are non-negligible; the rest are ~1e-16 and can be dropped.
Any mathematically equivalent evaluation is allowed (another basis or evaluation order), as long as it only uses these inputs.

Correctness: every output must be within 1e-06 (absolute) of the expected values on all test cases (fixed, dense). Timing is measured on the dense case.

# Baseline kernel
```cpp
// Baseline generated by agent/tasks/gen_baselines.py; Chebyshev relu degree 2 on [-4, 4], as in benchmarks/chebyshev_ckks.

void fhe()
{
  Ciphertext x("x");
  Plaintext alpha("alpha");
  Ciphertext z = x * alpha;
  Plaintext one("one");
  vector<Ciphertext> t(3);
  t[1] = z;
  Ciphertext z_square = z * z;
  t[2] = z_square + z_square - one;
  Ciphertext result;
  bool has_result = false;
  Plaintext c1("c1");
  Ciphertext term1 = t[1] * c1;
  result = has_result ? result + term1 : term1;
  has_result = true;
  Plaintext c2("c2");
  Ciphertext term2 = t[2] * c2;
  result = has_result ? result + term2 : term2;
  has_result = true;
  Plaintext c0("c0");
  result = result + c0;
  result.set_output("y");
}
```

